  <h2>2. What StockReclaim does — and does not do</h2>
  <p>
    The App audits your Shopify refunds and returns and lists the units that were
    refunded or returned but never put back into sellable inventory, with an age and
    a value for each case. It lets you mark a case resolved, write it off, or put the
    units back into inventory with <strong>Restock now</strong>. Depending on your
    plan it also sends a weekly digest email and a monthly reconciliation PDF.
  </p>
  <p>Please understand its limits:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>It audits returns; it does not manage them.</strong> It is not a returns portal, does not create labels and does not communicate with your customers.</li>
    <li><strong>It cannot see your shelf.</strong> The App reports where Shopify's records disagree with each other. It never asserts a physical count, and a case it lists is an indicator to check, not a proven loss.</li>
    <li><strong>Its findings depend on Shopify's data.</strong> Missing, delayed or incorrect data in your store produces missing or incorrect findings.</li>
    <li><strong>It is not accounting, tax or legal advice.</strong> Figures shown are working estimates from your order data; decide with your own records and advisers.</li>
    <li><strong>Restock now changes your inventory.</strong> It runs only when you click it on a specific case, and it does what the confirmation says. You are responsible for checking the case before you confirm.</li>
  </ul>

